diff --git a/CHANGELOG.md b/CHANGELOG.md
index 8d6d9ec..0680185 100644
--- a/CHANGELOG.md
+++ b/CHANGELOG.md
@@ -4,6 +4,17 @@ CarLink's releases, newest first. Versions follow `major.minor.patch`; each one
 [GitHub](https://github.com/F-e-n-y-x/CarLink/releases) with its APK. The text under each version
 is what the in-app update popup shows.
 
+## [Unreleased]
+
+- Wireless Android Auto no longer fails at once with "Wi-Fi Direct is in use by another app" when
+  an idle Wi-Fi Direct group from another app or an earlier session is left on the stereo (seen on a
+  Topway head unit): CarLink removes it and connects, as Open Headunit does.
+- Wireless Android Auto on head units whose own Bluetooth is already the phone's hands-free link:
+  when the phone does not start Android Auto by itself, CarLink now wakes it (at most twice per
+  connection) instead of waiting until it gives up. On Android 12 and older stereos with their own
+  hands-free Bluetooth, CarLink first turns the stereo's Bluetooth off and on once, so its hands-free
+  link reconnects and Android Auto starts; wireless Android Auto now waits up to 50 s for the phone.
+
 ## [1.0.6] - 2026-10-20
 
 - Faster connections: USB Android Auto in about 1.3 s (was 3.2 s), wireless Android Auto in about 3 s.
